{
  "dom_id": "step-37200",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying Data Sets That Could Be Normally Distributed",
  "problem": "Which of the following data sets **might** be normally distributed?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14266294/assets/d40721092d0e11fdc2ac582688491a922bd0c6240e5bfa44b6374a73f6577685.png)",
  "worked_solution": "If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. \n\nAmong the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is shown in diagram II:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14266294/assets/382e3bc616bc15ac99fb5f18f1f9a75925eb2b5760152c7088fdbc7047fff904.png)\n\nIt's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-37200\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"37200\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"9892\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-37200\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-2\">Identifying Data Sets That Could Be Normally Distributed</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"37200\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <p>Which of the following data sets <strong>might</strong> be normally distributed?</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-cdec8b9ece66152d62f2dbb412e1ffbd\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/cdec8b9ece66152d62f2dbb412e1ffbd\"></div>\n\n\n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <p>If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. </p>\n<p>Among the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is shown in diagram II:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-aaad3df612dabb3df1f8277d8a90f5d0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/aaad3df612dabb3df1f8277d8a90f5d0\"></div>\n\n<p>It's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.</p>\n\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
